.env

# There is deliberately no `*.png` rule here any more, and it must not come
# back. It existed to keep the ~100MB of test screenshots out of the build
# context, but `tests/` and `shoreline/` already do that wholesale -- and it
# carried `!template_18x18.png` / `!template_20x20.png` exceptions for the two
# renders the image used to COPY. Those files are deleted, so with the rule in
# place `COPY Overlays/` and `COPY Assets/` would have matched *nothing* and
# built an image with no board renders and no ruin sprite.
#
# That failure is now loud rather than silent -- polymerge has no legacy
# template to fall back on, so the bot refuses at startup instead of merging
# 18 and 20 against different fog art. It is still a failure worth not
# shipping. Everything the image needs is named explicitly by COPY, so this
# file only has to keep the context small.
